OL,3,GNEWSADisadvantaged pupils read less,
OL,4,Areport suggests
OL,5,
OL,6,FChildren from low income families in
OL,7,FJersey are less likely to read for
OL,8,Fpleasure than others, a new report has
OL,9,Fsuggested.
OL,11,FThe Open University spoke to about
OL,12,F4,500 young people aged seven to 14
OL,13,Fabout their reading habits and found
OL,14,F60% of them did not enjoy reading.
OL,16,FThe report indicated 27.2% of children
OL,17,Ffrom more affluent backgrounds enjoyed
OL,18,Freading, double the number of those
OL,19,Ffrom lower income homes where 13.4%
OL,20,Fread regularly.
OL,23,APub: 14-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
